+API test, and two comparator regressions. The API test covers decoded PASS
+commands, public state, terminal banks, and economic/attribution counters.
+Comparator tests reject private inventory insertion-order drift and public
+integer-versus-float drift. Replay tests compare complete public and private
+state, private shed/seeds/inventory key order, statuses, typed `Vec<f64>` rewards,
+step/done and terminal banks. Typed rewards accommodate recorded `[0,0]` versus
+serialized `[0.0,0.0]` without relaxing public market-number comparisons.
